{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSixteen surviving Python modules under `tests/unit` contain 27 audited prose blocks: 21 true leading docstrings and 6 full-line comment regions. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45`. The stable allowlist excludes deleted files while retaining current live prose.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the stable-ID blocks below. For every owned path, retain immutable before and final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only an allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` that is the first statement of a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining normalized ASTs to match.\n\nTokenize both blobs and reject every changed inline comment or non-allowlisted full-line comment. Preserve non-docstring runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/test_create_duplicate_warning.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_malformed_applies_to_rejected_at_overlay_load(tmp_path, bad_applies_to):`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_REPO_ROOT = str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2])`\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py` — 4 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_repository_wide_selects_on_empty_changed_files(tmp_path):`\n  - `D:test_repository_wide_selects_on_empty_changed_files`\n  - `D:test_code_review_project_det_is_exempt_from_nonempty_glob_rule`\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_criterion_effectiveness.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_cross_session_warn_routes.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_LITERAL_BEFORE = frozenset(`\n- `tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_fetch_diagnostics.py` — 4 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:TestRunGitSurfacesStderr.test_old_shape_is_the_negative_control`\n  - `D:test_store_copy_fixture_leaves_no_swallowed_diagnostic`\n  - `D:TestBridgeStateScrub.test_seed_unit_resurrects_the_cache_and_recommit_scrub_removes_it`\n- `tests/unit/test_decomp_shape_criterion.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_delivered_manifest_scan_count.py` — 2 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_delivered_manifest_scan_count_constant_in_child_count`\n- `tests/unit/test_delivered_now.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_delta_tree_timeout_b0e0.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_dependency_advisory_wiring.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py`: `C:test_registry_entries_well_formed:before:if entry.permanent:`\n- `tests/unit/test_description_cap_warning.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_det_floor_operator_attested.py` — 4 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_FIXTURES = [`\n  - `D:test_tag_regex_single_source`\n  - `D:test_agreement_with_workflow_ops`\n\n`D:<symbol>` is a true leading docstring. `C:<scope>:before:<code>` is one maximal full-line comment region anchored to unchanged code. No other prose is editable. In reviewer TSV, `stable_block_id` is the path-qualified `<path>#<D:...>` or `<path>#<C:...>` value.\n\n## Protected false positives\nAll unlisted prose and executable lines from the old spans are protected,  The two operator-attested IDs in the deleted `test_criterion_preview.py` have left current scope.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Creation/criteria prose keeps nonblocking duplicate advice; fail-closed overlay shape; repository-wide empty-change behavior; immutable snapshots; vocabulary exceptions; effectiveness reproducibility; preview outcomes; and sanitized project-criterion authoring.\n- Route/DC prose keeps route-derived warnings, the intentional policy baseline, stderr propagation, swallowed-diagnostic guards, and projects-seed scrub ordering.\n- Plan/completion prose keeps ADR-0111 canonical ownership, import seams, deterministic decomp shape, constant delivered-child scans, verified delivery, bounded delta fallback, and portable advisory wiring.\n- Deprecation/description/DET prose keeps an empty registry as valid, replacement rules for future entries, nonblocking cap warnings, clarity floors, and the current `decide_ops` identity/recognition contract.\n- All modules are direct pytest inputs. Mechanism baselines identify autouse fixtures; the criteria-vocabulary allowlist, decomp eval spec, portability/overlay tests, and `_deprecations.py` source guards reference these paths. No target import, `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Prose changes occur only inside the 27 declared stable-ID blocks.\n- [ ] Any changed blank line is adjacent to an edited stable-ID block.\n- [ ] The normalized-AST comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] The token/comment comparison passes on every owned path.\n- [ ] A non-author reviewer posts exactly 27 leaf-linked TSV rows, one for each declared stable-ID block.\n- [ ] Every reviewer row uses this schema: stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session.\n- [ ] Every before_citation equals 9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45:<path>#<stable-id>.\n- [ ] Every final_citation equals <final-commit-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>.\n- [ ] Every row record